     Spellbook fading has been buggy for a long time, possibly
since the initial implementation.  It works differently in the
post-3.4.3 code than it used to, and may or may not be fixed.
(I don't even remember what changes it has undergone....)

     Although the code to lose spells has no comments saying so,
I'm sure that only losing from the end of the list was a very
deliberate design decision.  That causes the casting letters for
lost spells to become invalid, and those for retained spells to
be the same as they were before amnesia.  So if the player casts
a spell using the letters as they were prior to amnesia, he won't
use a different spell than expected.  That wouldn't be the case
if spells were removed from throughout the list since doing such
would assign new letters to every spell past the first lost one.
(That could be handled by changing spell letters to work more
like inventory letters, but so far no one has done such a thing.)

     Forgetting spells has been changed to set the retention
amount to zero, same as happens when it's been too long since
you learned the spell.  No letters are reassigned, and the only
surprise to the player will be that some spells have worn out
earlier than anticipated.  Once on the known spell list, spells
will stay there regardless of amnesia.


